   "slug": "eurokon",
   "title": "Eurokon, 2. Symposium für interaktives Recycling",
   "year": "1996",
   "header": "Eurokon, 2. Symposium für interaktives Recycling, 1996",
   "bodytext_html": "Following the success of Eurokot, a second eight-week forum in Russia is organized with <br />cooperation by the Museum of Primitive Arts of Ural and Siberia, the association Environment <br />(state architecture and arts academy of Yekaterinburg), the Siberian Unesco club Krug and <br />the Swiss foundation pro Helvetia.<br /><br />This collective of artists, made up of 16 Western European and 10 Russian artists, met in <br />Yekaterinburg to work in groups with the raw waste material of four different factory areas <br />on site: one tyre production, a rubber factory, a ceramic foundry and a scrap yard. <br />Unfortunately, the physical exposition of the project is only documented by a gallery show in <br />town, as at the time, industrial locations were not accessible to the public.<br />For their next endeavor the group travels to Novosibirsk where an exposition is created with <br />on site paintings, objects and sculptures, which was then shown in the national museum of <br />Siberia.\r\n",
   "text_uid": 1239,
